<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 1.036 bln stg further.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 1.036 bln stg further.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 1.036 billion stg of assistance at established interest rates.  </p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1.5 BLN    1.5 BLN    1.5 BLN    =</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY     24 MLN    424 MLN    1.46 BLN  =</p>
<p> DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1 T BILLS	   =	     =	   3 MLN*   =</p>
<p> BAND 1 BANK BILLS	=	     =	 715 MLN*   =</p>
<p> BAND 2 BANK BILLS	=	   50 MLN*   318 MLN*   =</p>
<p> BILLS/FRG TO FEB 17   24 MLN!   350 MLN    =	    =</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE 5-15/16 (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATE)</p>
<p>! INTEREST RATE 5-31/32 (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
